[h1]Recurring Diplomacy by Najane[/h1]

Diplomatic agreements in Civilization VII run out - Open Borders, Research Collaboration, Counterspy and the rest last a set number of turns, and then you have to remember to propose them again. This mod remembers for you.

[b]No rules change.[/b] Every proposal it sends is one you could make yourself from the Diplomacy screen, at the same Influence price, and the other leader can still say no.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]What you get[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One click to keep it running[/b] - a sync button beside every treaty, endeavour and espionage action on a leader's Diplomacy screen. Gold and glowing = on, grey = off.
[*][b]Starts right away[/b] - switching it on starts the action at once, if the game allows it now.
[*][b]Renewed as soon as it expires[/b] - proposed again at the start of your turn, the moment the game allows it.
[*][b]Plays by the game's limits[/b] - treaties can run with every leader; endeavours and espionage only with as many at once as the game allows (Benjamin Franklin gets an extra endeavour). A full limit locks the button and its tooltip names the leader it runs with; [b]Shift+click[/b] moves it to the leader you are talking to.
[*][b]You always know what happened[/b] - at the start of your turn a short summary lists what was renewed, grouped by leader with their portrait: [b]green[/b] agreed, [b]red[/b] refused, [b]grey[/b] no answer yet, [b]blue[/b] espionage. Hover it to keep it on screen.
[*][b]Saved with your game[/b] - load an older save and you get exactly the choices it had.
[/list]

Nothing is renewed until you switch it on: a fresh install changes nothing.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Languages[/h2]

English, German, Spanish, French, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, Ukrainian (shown when the game is set to Russian), Simplified and Traditional Chinese.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

UI only: [b]no rules, values or balance change[/b]. Your choices are stored in the save.

[hr][/hr]
